# Open-source provenance

CJ-DocGuard authored sources: Apache-2.0; no third-party Cangjie package dependencies.
Cangjie SDK/std.ast: external official runtime/toolchain, not bundled; see docs/toolchains.md.
Python standard library and system C compiler: development/protocol tooling, not vendored.
Integration source checkouts are fetched at exact commits listed in integrations/upstream-lock.json,
kept in ignored local build/cache directories, and retain original LICENSE notices.
leven4cj: Apache-2.0; is-png-cj and compare-versions-cj: MIT.
The executable integration harness samples are newly authored. Reviewed pinned upstream
cache checkouts and the lock file remain unchanged. By default copied upstream sources
also remain unchanged. Explicit --apply-reviewed-fixes creates a separately marked local
leven4cj copy with two Unicode empty-string branch repairs; it never patches the cache.
The reviewed patch, original/modified SHA-256 hashes and provenance are recorded in
integrations/leven4cj/patches/ and each generated provenance.json.
Apache-2.0 LICENSE and available NOTICE files are preserved in the generated copy.
See docs/real-library-unicode-repair-2026-10-29.md for scope and reproduction commands.
No upstream project adoption, endorsement, or contributor status is implied.
